<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Jawa_BackgroundWater — a biome that NO TILE WILL EVER HAVE.

    It exists for exactly one field read, in exactly one place:
      WorldDrawLayer_Terrain.cs:48
        req.secondaryTex = planetLayer.Def.backgroundBiome.DrawMaterial.mainTexture;

    That is how RimWorld paints the water half of every TerrainMask landmark —
    Peninsula, Bay, CoastalIsland. It takes the background biome's RAW TEXTURE and
    bypasses the shader entirely.

    🔴 WHY OURS AND NOT Ocean. `RW - Planet Atmosphere` (workshop 3272330410)
    repoints Ocean.texture AND Lake.texture at `TerrainReplace/Water`, which is a
    1x1 PNG of RGB(0,0,0) — measured, 119 bytes on disk. So every cape on the
    planet paints its sea with one black pixel. The OPEN ocean looks correct
    because its colour comes from the WorldOcean SHADER reading per-vertex
    elevation; the landmark path never touches the shader. Two code paths, one
    texture, and only one of them was ever going to look right.
    ⛔ Do not "fix" this by repatching Ocean.texture. That material draws the whole
    sea, and the Atmosphere mod flattened it deliberately.

    ⚠️ `implemented` false keeps it out of worldgen biome scoring. `isBackgroundBiome`
    true matches Ocean and Lake, and matters only to LandmarkDef.IsValidTile — which
    can never see it, because no tile carries this biome.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>Jawa_BackgroundWater</defName>
    <label>mineral water</label>
    <description>Sediment-laden, mineral-saturated and faintly toxic. The water of Ash'karr carries more suspended rock than life.</description>
    <implemented>false</implemented>
    <isBackgroundBiome>true</isBackgroundBiome>
    <canBuildBase>false</canBuildBase>
    <canAutoChoose>false</canAutoChoose>
    <allowRoads>false</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <texture>World/Biomes/Jawa_SickWater</texture>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
